    <!--
      Unavailable, not failed. The user cannot fix any of these by retyping,
      which is why Bit shows a different face for them: a dry face the user
      can act on teaches them to read it, and one they cannot teaches them to
      ignore it.

      These take no format arguments. A surface knows which command it is
      answering about but not what the user typed, and echoing the parse back
      on "no wifi panel" would be noise. The commands where seeing the parse
      matters are the long locks, and those echo it in the confirmation.
    -->
